[836.616304, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        Wait until all the runner subprocesses have exited, restarting them if\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        necessary and configured to do so.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        \"\"\"\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        log = logging.getLogger('mailman.runner')\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        log.info('Master started')\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        self._pause()\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m        while True:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m            try:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m                pid, status = os.wait()\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[3m... (81 lines hidden, /toggle to show all)\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m@click.command(\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    cls=I18nCommand,\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    context_settings=dict(help_option_names=['-h', '--help']),\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    help=_(\"\"\"\\\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    Master subprocess watcher.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[836.616362, "o", "    \u001b[2m    Start and watch the configured runners, ensuring that they stay alive and\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    kicking.  Each runner is forked and exec'd in turn, with the master waiting\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    on their process ids.  When it detects a child runner has exited, it may\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m    restart it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
